    description: "**Mechanic**: Five linker families (graphql_resolver, graphql, http, event_sourcing, message_queue) emit a cross-language boolean and four sibling meta keys on 29 edges. The meta-key registry (`MetaKeySpec`) contains ~30 entries; a grep for the five emitted keys returns one hit, and that one is a different key (`channel_kind`, not the emitted `channel`). The axis-comment rule on dataclass fields does not apply because these are inside `meta: Dict`; the parallel registry that does cover meta-bag keys lacks entries for all five.\n\n**Expectation**: Every meta-bag key emitted by any producer is registered in `MetaKeySpec` (or equivalent), so the writer-contract validator and consumer-side registry-drift check both police the key.\n\n**Scope**: 5 unregistered meta keys emitted on 29 edges by 5 linker families.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer relying on `validation_report.writer_contract` or `axis_conformance` to catch unknown meta keys; any future addition that depends on the registry for vocabulary discovery.\n\n**Consequence**: Schema-conformance audits miss the unregistered keys silently; the writer-contract bucket reports zero violations when there are 29 emitted but unregistered key-instances per edge × multiple keys.\n\n**Source**: F54.A2 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 8494
    fields: {}  # 8494
